{"study_accession":"PRJNA812498","secondary_study_accession":"SRP362307","title":"CAR Density Influences Antitumoral Efficacy of BCMA CAR T Cells and Correlates with Clinical Outcome [RNA-seq]","description":"In this work, we address the impact of CAR density on the in vitro and in vivo functionality of BCMA-CAR T cells. Phenotypic, functional, transcriptomic and epigenomic studies at bulk and single cell level revealed different profiles between CAR T cells with high and low expression of the CAR molecule (CARHigh and CARLow T cells). We analyzed the phenotype of CARHigh and CARLow T cell populations before and after stimulation with tumor cells. Sorted CD4+ and CD8+ CARHigh and CARLow T cell populations from six different CAR T cell productions were profiled using high-throughput RNA sequencing (RNA-seq) and assay for transposase-accessible chromatin (ATAC-seq). To better understand the heterogeneity of CAR T cells and the influence of CAR level on their transcriptomic profile, we performed single cell transcriptomic analysis on 43,981 CAR T cells from three independent productions. Overall design: We have carried out a comprehensive study of the influence of CAR density in CAR T cell function. We have performed transcriptomic assays at bulk level in FACS-isolated subpopulations of CAR-T cells with different CAR densities.","pubmed":"36179026","geo_series":"","n_samples":24,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN26417584","study_accession":"PRJNA812498","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"D9_Low_CD8_S14_R1_001 [RNA-seq]","description":"D9_Low_CD8_S14_R1_001 [RNA-seq]","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM5931303","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-10-06","attributes":[["source_name","Donor cells"],["diagnosis","Healthy"],["tissue","Blood"],["cell_type","D9_Low_CD8 CAR T cells"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR18212590","experiment_accession":"SRX14359155","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrum